nala (0.17.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  The Python-only --raw-dpkg mode is retired; use plain output for log-friendly
  transactions. The no-op --license and download --fetch options are also
  removed. License information remains available in the package copyright
  file.

 -- Blake Lee <blake@volian.org>  Tue, 01 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0500

nala (0.17.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  This package now builds the Rust implementation of Nala.

  /etc/nala/nala.conf remains TOML, with new Ui and Color sections for the Rust
  implementation. It remains a dpkg conffile: dpkg replaces an unmodified
  packaged file automatically and prompts before replacing local changes. If
  the old file is kept, the packaged file is normally saved as
  /etc/nala/nala.conf.dpkg-dist. Nala now refuses an existing invalid config or
  retired field instead of silently using defaults.

  Plain output and binary units are now the defaults. The TUI is opt-in through
  Ui.mode or --tui. Legacy scrolling_text and transfer_speed_bits settings are
  retired; Ui.mode = "Plain" is the log-friendly output mode.

  Legacy Python history is read automatically and imported on the first
  history mutation. The original history.json file is preserved.

 -- Blake Lee <blake@volian.org>  Wed, 20 May 2026 00:00:00 -0500

nala (0.15.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  Nala hooks have been removed. You should use apt hooks.

 -- Blake Lee <blake@volian.org>  Tue, 23 Jan 2024 23:37:08 -0600

nala (0.9.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  The configuration file for Nala at `/etc/nala/nala.conf`
  has been changed to toml. This change is BREAKING as the older config
  file will no longer work. Nala will still run with the old config,
  but there will be a syntax error and it will use the program defaults.

 -- Blake Lee <blake@volian.org>  Mon, 23 May 2022 15:53:49 -0400
